o A1 to B2 is adjacent — no space, so no flip (only if B2 were @ and further *)  \n  So only confirmed flip is B1 via vertical (south) direction. So (A,1) flips B1.\n\n- (A,4): Currently empty. Check surroundings. North: out. South: B4=@, C4=*, so A4→B4→C4: @ between A4(*) and C4(*) → flips B4.  \n  West: A3=@, A2=@, A1=. → but A1 is empty, so no closure from west.  \n  East: A5=@, A6=@, A7=@, A8=. → ends at empty, no closure.  \n  Diagonals: SW? B3=@, C2=*, so A4→B3→C2: @ at B3, * at C2 — yes, if aligned. A4 to B3 is southeast? No: A4 to B3 is south-west? Let's coordinate:  \n  A4 → B3 is (row+1, col-1)? No: A to B is +1 row, 4 to 3 is -1 col → that’s southwest. But standard directions: from A4, southwest is invalid (no row below A). Wait: A is first row, so south is increasing row. So from A4, south is B4, C4, etc. Southwest would be B3, then C2, D1.  \n  So A4 → B3 (@), C2 (*) → yes, path: A4(*), B3(@), C2(*) → sandwiches B3. So flips B3.  \n  Also, south: A4→B4(@), C4(*) → flips B4.  \n  So (A,4) flips both B4 and B3. Possibly more?  \n  Southeast: A4→B5→C6→D7→E8: B5=@, C6=@, D7=@, E8=* → so A4(*), B5(@), C6(@), D7(@), E8(*) → this line connects! So flips B5, C6, D7.  \n  That’s significant: three more pieces flipped.  \n  So total flips for (A,4): B3 (SW), B4 (S), and B5,C6,D7 (SE). That’s 1 + 1 + 3 = 5 pieces flipped. Very strong.\n\n- (A,8): Empty. Check directions.  \n  West: A7=@, A6=@, A5=@, A4=. → A4 is empty, so no closure from west.  \n  South: B8=*, already mine — adjacent. So A8 to B8 is south, B8=*, no opponent in between → no flip.  \n  Southwest: B7=@, C6=@, D5=*, so A8→B7→C6→D5: A8(*), B7(@), C6(@), D5(*) → yes, sandwiches B7 and C6. Flips two.  \n  So (A,8) flips B7 and C6.\n\n- (H,8): Currently empty.  \n  North: G8=@, F8=*, so H8→G8→F8: G8=@, F8=* → sandwiches G8. Flip one.  \n  West: H7=@, H6=@, H5=* → H8 to H7 to H6 to H5: H8(*), H7(@), H6(@), H5(*) → sandwiches H7 and H6. Flip two.  \n  Northwest: G7=@, F6=@, E5=*, so H8→G7→F6→E5: H8(*), G7(